{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## CURRENT STATUS — 45 descendants, 6 open, 0 uncertified. What remains, and why.\n\nThe tree has grown from 41 to **45** as Jira DC bugs are reparented in. Re-enumerated just now.\n\n### The certification blocker is CLEARED\n\n**0 descendants are closed-without-attestation.** The two that were — `0059` and `2bc7` — are\nreopened per the operator's ruling that a close without completion verification is prohibited.\nThat was the entire reason `certifiable` was False and this epic's signature was withheld\n(`gate_ops.py:129`). Both must be re-closed **on their own merits** through a working gate; the\ngate itself was repaired by [rebar:1019-e1e9-5117-4795] (Gerrit 1361, LLM-Review +1).\n\n### The 6 open children\n\n    0059  DC inbound filing is a no-op in live CI              REOPENED (was uncertified)\n    2bc7  Test helpers return an unregistered copy of mutation REOPENED (was uncertified)\n    2e47  rebar's hardcoded Jira vocabularies disagree with DC named by the completion verifier\n    275e  Probe whether /rest/api/2/applicat…                  reparented in\n    59b2  Live DC suite: residual assertions that cannot…      reparented in\n    d582  Rekey live cell can derive a colliding project…      reparented in\n\n`2e47` is not incidental: when the completion verifier could finally see, it named that bug as\nindicting this epic's subtree. It is the capability map's own output — `IDEA` status absent from\nevery DC workflow, label limit 254 not 255, duplicate `Task` issue types.\n\n### The epic's own ACs: 12 of 13\n\n**AC4 is UNTICKED and should stay that way until it is real.** The `[operator-attested]` bidirectional-\nreconcile criterion was failed by the completion verifier — it cites a run at an old sha — and my\nindependent read-only verification pass flagged the identical gap separately: this epic carries a\n`plan-review` attestation and **no completion/operator attestation**. Two independent checks, same\nconclusion.\n\nThe other 12 are MET with cited evidence (file:line or command output), including AC1's Gerrit half\nverified directly: all 11 changes this epic landed carry `Verified +1` AND `LLM-Review +1`.\n\n### Why the earlier close was wrong — the part worth not forgetting\n\nIt was not merely missing a signature. The verdict itself was wrong, in the permissive direction:\n\n    BEFORE the max_tokens fix   128 provider 400s, 32/32 epic-bug-screens FAILED  ->  PASS\n    AFTER                         0 provider 400s,  0 failures                    ->  FAIL\n\nEvery bug-screen call was 400ing and each failure degrades to \"unrelated\", so the caused_by bug\nfloor evaluated nothing and reported no findings. `2e47` was invisible for exactly as long as the\nscreen was blind.\n\n### Related, tracked outside the tree\n\n    1019  the max_tokens clamp — FIXED, Gerrit 1361 awaiting Verified\n    4b9e  re-home the outbound parent-CLEAR cell — probe pushed, Gerrit 1359\n    2a76  silent auto-push rejection + unscanned ticket payloads (from the credentials incident)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785860462857234001,"uuid":"407652fe-7d3f-4651-a3f7-d1e1eda1e67d"}